Quintessentia
Copyright 2026 Quintessentia contributors

Quintessentia is an
independent experimental inference engine built around pure-math mirror equality
scales, Q1 binary-halving crystals, self-contained NVRTC CUDA kernels, and
bounded streaming execution.

Historical upstream acknowledgments (for early streaming / placement / MTP
concepts retained in legacy modes):

- AirLLM — Gavin Li (lyogavin) and contributors:
  https://github.com/lyogavin/airllm
- Colibrì — Vincenzo Fornaro (JustVugg) and contributors:
  https://github.com/JustVugg/colibri

Upstream sources are not vendored here. An optional native tier library, when
present locally, is built from Colibrì's original tier.h; its license and notice
apply to it. Original upstream marks and names remain associated with their
respective authors and do not imply endorsement.

The Quintessentia mark (`assets/quintessentia-logo.png`) is an original project
emblem; see `assets/README.md`.
